[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am working on a PR to mathlib (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37189\">#37189</a>) and I just updated the cache and now I'm getting a <code>ProofWidgets not up-to-date</code> error. I tried running <code>lake exe cache get</code> again and it did not fix the issue. The error message says to report this issue on Zulip.</p>",
        "id": 582638392,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1774898013
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Try <code>lake build -H</code>.</p>",
        "id": 582638456,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1774898038
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That fixed it, thank you!</p>",
        "id": 582638576,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1774898086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(This problem is going away soon! We have redundant fixes landed in both lake and ProofWidgets.)</p>",
        "id": 582659233,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774906807
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a fix for when this happens during CI (this just happened in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35790\">#35790</a>)</p>",
        "id": 582696317,
        "sender_full_name": "Brian Nugent",
        "timestamp": 1774927375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, could you try merging <code>master</code> again? There was another CI change to proofwidgets in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37290\">#37290</a>. cc: <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"128280\">@𝚠𝚘𝚓𝚌𝚒𝚎𝚌𝚑 𝚗𝚊𝚠𝚛𝚘𝚌𝚔𝚒</span></p>",
        "id": 582696625,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryan Gin-ge Chen",
        "timestamp": 1774927574
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm running into the same issue; I have tried</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">stderr</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">✖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">441</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">596</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Building</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proofwidgets</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">widgetJsAll</span>\n<span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofWidgets</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">date</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Please</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cache</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fetch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">latest</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProofWidgets</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">If</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">work</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">report</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">your</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">issue</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Zulip</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">required</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targets</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">logged</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failures</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proofwidgets</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">widgetJsAll</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dependencies</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rm -rf .lake lake-manifest.json</code></li>\n<li><code>lake exe cache get!</code> (multiple times)</li>\n<li><code>lake build -H</code> (this was mentioned in another thread)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Any other advice?</p>",
        "id": 597666048,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam",
        "timestamp": 1779731463
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Have you merged master before deleting .lake?</p>",
        "id": 597668005,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1779732464
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You should not remove <code>lake-manifest.json</code>. If this was on a git repository, <code>git restore lake-manifest.json</code> should bring it back.</p>",
        "id": 597669774,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1779733407
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unless I'm misunderstanding what \"merged master\" means, I'm using the 4.28.0 version of Mathlib and Lean; my <code>lakefile.toml</code> contains</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"mathlib\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4.git\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"v4.28.0\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597670820,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam",
        "timestamp": 1779734059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is an older version, try <code>lake update</code> and then <code>lake exe cache get!</code></p>",
        "id": 597672124,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1779734786
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry about that <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"928928\">@Sam</span>! 4.28.0 is indeed an older version, you may be running into an issue that was fixed later, perhaps hash reuse but it's hard to say. Are you able to move to a more recent version (4.30.0-rc2) or is that difficult?</p>",
        "id": 597680427,
        "sender_full_name": "𝚠𝚘𝚓𝚌𝚒𝚎𝚌𝚑 𝚗𝚊𝚠𝚛𝚘𝚌𝚔𝚒",
        "timestamp": 1779739573
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I probably have to stay on 4.28.0 for now. :( </p>\n<p>However, the problem went away when I recreated the Lean project in a different folder on my computer. Is there any other persistent state in a Lean project besides the <code>.lake</code> folder that could cause this?</p>",
        "id": 597908206,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam",
        "timestamp": 1779818007
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not to my knowledge. Newer versions of Lean/Lake have a global cache directory, but 4.28 does not.</p>",
        "id": 597915073,
        "sender_full_name": "𝚠𝚘𝚓𝚌𝚒𝚎𝚌𝚑 𝚗𝚊𝚠𝚛𝚘𝚌𝚔𝚒",
        "timestamp": 1779819739
    }
]